      },
      "message": "feat(post): G41/G42 cutter compensation on Haas, Mazak and Siemens 840D\n\nHaas and Mazak write the Fanuc-family words on the next straight feed\nblock (G1/G01 G41|G42 ... D<tool>, G40 on the lead-out); Siemens 840D\nwrites G1 G41|G42 NORM with the radius from the edge the tool call\nalready selected (T n D n). The Fanuc post's laws carry over: a comp\nword on a rapid, an arc or past the section end, or inside a canned\ncycle, is a named refusal that blocks the gate; wear (#38) writes one\nregister note per section. Heidenhain keeps its by-name refusal - its\ndocumented engage point is not stated against the next element, and\nits radius is always R plus DR (docs/decisions/39-comp-dialects.md).\n\nGoldens: golden/nc/{haas,mazak,sinumerik}/contour_{control,wear}_comp.nc.\n\nFixes #39\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
